# 4. Three-case state machine — bench/references.md §4, Phase-1 surface:
#
#   λx0:Num. if x0 == 0 then 1 else if x0 == 1 then 2 else 0
#
# Note the comparisons are typed *operator first* (`=` at the empty hole,
# then its operands). Typing `x0` first would also work — the editor never
# refuses — but in a branch whose sibling is already a `Num` it would make
# the branch transiently `Bool`, which the calculus quarantines: `⦇x0 == 1⦈`,
# to be unwrapped later with Enter. Operator-first is the cheaper route here,
# and it is the same number of keystrokes.

\
x
0
:
n
.

# if x0 == 0 then 1 else ⦇⦈
=          # ⦇⦈ == ⦇⦈, cursor on the left operand
x
0
tab        # → the right operand
0
?          # climbs out of the `==` and wraps it as the scrutinee
1
tab        # → the else branch

# else if x0 == 1 then 2 else 0
?          # a nested conditional, cursor on its scrutinee
=
x
0
tab
1
tab        # → the then branch
2
tab        # → the else branch
0
